** Help Monitoring Strategy 1: Implicit Observations **

MTSS based solution + Impasse-Driven problem solving

if a participant is taking more than 3+ minutes on completing a task:
    the system should send a probing message to the user

    if the particpant needs help:
        refer to the help tree

    if the participant does not need help:
        the system should continue monitoring

    !!!
    Why: According to the literature of Impasse-Driven problem solving a fast
    impasse yields better results in terms of both insight and solution
    !!!

if a participant is testing the same function more than 7 times:
    the system should send a probing message to the user

    if the particpant needs help:
        refer to the help tree

    if the participant does not need help:
        the system should continue monitoring


    !!!
    Why: According to the literature of MTSS progression monitoring is key in
    preventing negative work outcomes
    !!!

if a participant has a help counter of more than 3:
    the system should set a timer and signal teammates to check-in with the
    struggling teammate


if the particpant needs help:

    if the participant needs any amount of help completing the task:
        the system should notify teammates that are waiting

        if no teammates are done with their tasks:
            the system should analyze the state of each teammates on the tree if
            a teammate has completed more tasks (if both teammates have the same
            amount of tasks completed pick one) and is moving down the tree send
            a notification

            the system should note down who has been helped

    if teammates cannot/refuse to help:
        the system should notify the requester that no available resources

        if there is another task available high up on the task priority
        tree:
            the system can propose to reallocate the work to a task that is
            higher on the priority tree


** Help Monitoring Strategy 2: Code State Observations **

// find theory such as codellaborator but team based

if a participant is less than than 70% done with the task after 5 minutes:
    the system should send a probing message to the user

    if the particpant needs help:
        refer to the help tree

    if the participant does not need help:
        the system should reset the monitoring timer for a short amount of time

if a participant is testing the same function more than 7 times:
    the system should send a probing message to the user

    if the particpant needs help:
        refer to the help tree

    if the participant does not need help:
        the system should reset the monitoring timer for a short amount of time

if the particpant needs help:

    if the participant needs a lot of help completing the task:
        the system should notify teammates that are done with their task to
        assist the struggling teammate

        if no teammates are done with their tasks:
            the system should analyze the state of each teammates code and check
            for less than 10% or more than 90% completion and send a notification
            to that teammate

    if the participant needs a moderate amount of help completing the task:
        the system should notify teammates that are done with their task to
        assist the struggling teammate

        if no teammates are done with their tasks:
            the system should analyze the state of each teammates code and check
            for less than 20% or more than 75% completion and send a notification

    if the partipcant needs a small amount of help completing the task:
        the system should send a notification to any teammate as the
        interruption time should be minimal

    if teammates cannot/refuse to help:
        the system should notify the requester that no available resources

        if there is another task available high up on the task priority
        tree:
            the system can propose to reallocate the work to a task that is
            higher on the priority tree


if an individual asks explicitly for help:
  do protocol for help based on monitoring pattern
